<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Lakeshore Tour (Clear Lake from Clear Lake Sno-Park)</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:165-2: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.194570" lon="-121.692450"><ele>1166.2</ele><name>Clear Lake Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:clear-lake-sno-park; DEM 3,826 ft, the book's figure exactly; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 163; book_elev_ft: 3826; quote: CLEAR LAKE SNO-PARK 3826'</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.184970" lon="-121.693827"><ele>1108.7</ele><name>Road 2630 turns west (0.8 mi)</name><desc>source: OSM: Forest Road 2630 (way 1497150717) ends where it turns west and an unnamed paved road (way 1497150718) carries on south to the campground; confidence: high; pdf_page: 167; quote: From Clear Lake Sno-Park ski down Road 2630 0.8 mile then turn right (still on 2630) [Westside Tour]</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.178050" lon="-121.697096"><ele>1072.9</ele><name>Boat ramp and campground</name><desc>source: lake end of the paved OSM service road 283547879 in Clear Lake Campground, 8 m from the water; DEM 3,520 ft = the book's lake level; 0.55 mi along the shore to the dam; confidence: high; pdf_page: 167; book_elev_ft: 3520; quote: follow Road 2630 1.2 miles to the shoreline boat ramp and campground, a gentle descent</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.174867" lon="-121.688438"><ele>1074.4</ele><name>Dam</name><desc>source: shore line at the east end of the USGS NHD Clear Lake polygon, by the OSM Wasco Dam (way 934164397); confidence: high; pdf_page: 167; quote: It is 0.7 mile to the dam at the lake's east end along either the road or shoreline</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.179009" lon="-121.727902"><ele>1073.2</ele><name>West end of the lake</name><desc>source: westmost point of the shore line, where the inlet streams come in; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 167; quote: Crossing inlet streams may offer small but surmountable problems</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.192501" lon="-121.718413"><ele>1073.8</ele><name>Head of the north arm</name><desc>source: northmost point of the shore line; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 167; quote: The north arm of the lake is especially lovely</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.178050" lon="-121.697096"><ele>1072.9</ele><name>Boat ramp and campground (return)</name><desc>source: as above; confidence: high; pdf_page: 167</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.184970" lon="-121.693827"><ele>1108.7</ele><name>Road 2630 turns west (return)</name><desc>source: as above; confidence: high; pdf_page: 167</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.194570" lon="-121.692450"><ele>1166.2</ele><name>Clear Lake Sno-Park (finish)</name><desc>source: as start; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 163; book_elev_ft: 3826</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Lakeshore Tour (Clear Lake from Clear Lake Sno-Park)</name><desc>1. Clear Lake Sno-Park -&gt; Road 2630 turns west (0.8 mi): osm (high), 0.73 mi | 2. Road 2630 turns west (0.8 mi) -&gt; Boat ramp and campground: osm (high), 0.51 mi | 3. Boat ramp and campground -&gt; Dam: line (medium), 0.57 mi | 4. Dam -&gt; West end of the lake: line (medium), 2.37 mi | 5. West end of the lake -&gt; Head of the north arm: line (medium), 2.05 mi | 6. Head of the north arm -&gt; Boat ramp and campground (return): line (medium), 2.08 mi | 7. Boat ramp and campground (return) -&gt; Road 2630 turns west (return): osm (high), 0.51 mi | 8. Road 2630 turns west (return) -&gt; Clear Lake Sno-Park (finish): osm (high), 0.73 mi</desc>
